      "message": "fix(verify): a feed move into carried stock outside the declared stock refuses the post\n\nPR #410 review, finding 3: the overhang note was advisory, but the op\nmachines only its declared stock, so a feed move (lead-in, side offset,\nplunge, or the tool body under the carried top) reaching carried\nmaterial outside it engages stock nothing verified. Such a path now\ncarries CARRIED_OUTSIDE_DECLARED, naming both setups, the overhang and\nthe first move that reaches it. The post gate refuses on it by name\n(operation::carried_problems) and tells the user to enlarge the later\nsetup's stock. The reach test reads the carried grid's columns under\neach feed chord's footprint box, falling back to the body's box when\nthe grid is unreadable. An overhang no feed move reaches is only noted\n(CARRIED_OUTSIDE_NOTED).\n\nPins: the refusal and the plain note; a Setup1 change restamps a\nnon-rest op and a posed op whose job stock grew; single-setup and\nclip-entered stamps never read the carry.\n\nRefs #319\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
